 this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.583)=0.010.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.583.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162101 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82f2479b-d8f2-5042-a571-7ba4c713dad8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a T-Score Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d802cd-4b67-578a-a4f0-3a121dd507f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.602" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159405} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a863d1-a2f3-5551-ada5-acf3dba33b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.921" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159406} {:answer/id #uuid "1a816fa4-18ae-5b08-950b-07e1cfa1fc9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.341" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159407} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc62c9a-7251-5048-ab6a-64ade36d726f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.753" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159408} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7b0c11-16bc-586f-876c-b3cd9f184182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.898" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dc62c9a-7251-5048-ab6a-64ade36d726f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.753" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159408} :answer-field/id #uuid "6064d4e4-2052-59d2-a9ba-e12f8f88b464" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d00e7464-784c-509a-85ce-ef78495e5c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-142458" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ wher