.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{19},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=19.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $19$ | $1.328$ | $1.729$ | $2.093$ | $2.539$ | $2.861$ |\n| $20$ | $1.325$ | $1.725$ | $2.086$ | $2.528$ | $2.845$ |\n| $21$ | $1.323$ | $1.721$ | $2.080$ | $2.518$ | $2.831$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.861)=0.005.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.861.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6665557-2c04-5082-ba56-28f9376f00e6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a T-Score Using Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54111d63-60c2-50d4-a986-69633e4c59d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.796" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499816} {:answer/id #uuid "59de7596-9c87-5e83-86a1-c76e8e1bd1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.228" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499827} {:answer/id #uuid "90553719-cd64-556f-aa65-00d0d8df028a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499934} {:answer/id #uuid "af653e45-d79f-52af-a984-f7d63322f2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.106" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500004} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb3d4c9-bc0d-5373-bbd4-413f74299d1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.782" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90553719-cd64-556f-aa65-00d0d8df028a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499934} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5d5597-da21-5f7e-975e-6917a842fec7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db