rm $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|X|>x) & =1-P(|X|\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.9 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/63/635de7075b0d106ffc2a0f15e65ca7a3406a49945591aa5eae59090c74df1398.png)\n\nDue to the symmetry of the student's $t$-distribution, we have that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.1$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2P(X\\ge x)=0.1\\,⟹\\,P(X\\ge x)=0.05.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{20},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=20.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $19$ | $1.328$ | $1.729$ | $2.093$ | $2.539$ | $2.861$ |\n| $20$ | $1.325$ | $1.725$ | $2.086$ | $2.528$ | $2.845$ |\n| $21$ | $1.323$ | $1.721$ | $2.080$ | $2.518$ | $2.831$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 1.725)=0.050.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.725.$"}]}
